/page --style corporate --spacing default

/hero --bg gradient {
  /text "Design System Demo" --bold --size 2.5rem --color white
  /text "Corporate style + default spacing" --color white --italic
}

## Style Presets

Apply a style preset to change the entire visual identity of your document. This document uses `--style corporate`.

/columns 2 --gap 2rem {

  /card --icon star {
    ### Corporate

    Deep blue primary, Inter font, tight 0.25rem border radius. Professional and restrained.

    /code polyester {
      /page A4 --style corporate
    }
  }

  /card --icon bolt {
    ### Playful

    Purple accent on warm background, Nunito font, generous 1rem border radius.

    /code polyester {
      /page A4 --style playful
    }
  }

}

## Spacing Comparison

The spacing preset controls density. Compare `compact` vs `spacious`:

/columns 2 --gap 2rem {

  /frame --border "2px solid #e2e8f0" --padding 1.5rem --radius 8px {
    /text "Compact" --bold --size 1.1rem

    /table --header --bordered {
      Token | Value
      base | 0.75rem
      page-margin | 1.5cm
      section-gap | 1rem
      column-gap | 1rem
    }

    Dense documents, data tables, dashboards.
  }

  /frame --border "2px solid #e2e8f0" --padding 1.5rem --radius 8px {
    /text "Spacious" --bold --size 1.1rem

    /table --header --bordered {
      Token | Value
      base | 1.25rem
      page-margin | 3cm
      section-gap | 3rem
      column-gap | 2rem
    }

    Presentations, reports, marketing.
  }

}

## Composing via CLI

Mix any style with any spacing from the command line:

/code bash {
  # Corporate style, compact spacing
  poly build report.poly --style corporate --spacing compact

  # Playful style, spacious layout
  poly build invite.poly --style playful --spacing spacious

  # Dark mode, default spacing
  poly build slides.poly --style dark --spacing default

  # List available presets
  poly style list
  poly spacing list
}

## Inline CSS Overrides

Override individual tokens with `/style` for one-off adjustments:

/style {
  .custom-accent {
    --poly-color-primary: #e11d48;
    --poly-radius: 1rem;
  }
}

/region --bg #fef2f2 --padding 2rem {
  This region demonstrates that you can combine preset styles with inline CSS variable overrides for full control.
}

